        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): auto-generate session titles via AI summarization",
        "body": "Closes #77165\nRelated #89705\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nResolves a problem where users with many saved sessions had to identify sessions from truncated first-message text or session-id style fallbacks, making session history harder to scan and search.\n\nThe previous generated-title work also needed the generated title to behave consistently across the gateway session list, search, session-change events, Control UI filtering/patching, and the agent-facing `sessions_list` tool.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds an opt-in `sessionTitle` configuration and persists generated session titles as `autoTitle` metadata. Manual/display titles keep precedence, existing sessions without generated titles keep their current fallback behavior, and the feature remains default-off.\n\nThe title is derived from the same stored metadata across gateway, UI, and agent-facing session list paths. Background title generation uses the session model/auth context, not a separate public SDK selector path, and the public plugin SDK runtime-auth helper only accepts public parameters.\n\nThe update also avoids carrying transcript-derived generated titles into a new session after reset/new/rollover and guards async title writes so a title generated for an old `sessionId` is not written after the same `sessionKey` rotates to a new session.\n\nOut of scope: manual rename UI, migration/backfill for existing sessions, default-enabling generated titles, and new provider/channel/plugin capabilities.\n\n## User Impact\n\nWhen `sessionTitle.enabled` is on, users can get concise generated session titles instead of only first-message/session-id fallbacks. Session search can match those generated titles, already-open session lists can receive the post-write update, and agents using `sessions_list` see the same generated title users see.\n\nUsers who do not enable `sessionTitle` keep the existing behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal local gateway proof after the patch:\n\n```text\nValidation `local-gateway-session-title-proof-final` (pass, exit_code=0, 92583ms):\n\n[provider-transport-fetch] [model-fetch] start provider=deepseek api=openai-completions model=deepseek-chat method=POST url=https://api.deepseek.com/v1/chat/completions timeoutMs=undefined proxy=env policy=custom\n[provider-transport-fetch] [model-fetch] response provider=deepseek api=openai-completions model=deepseek-chat status=200 elapsedMs=543 contentType=text/event-stream; charset=utf-8\nproof=local-gateway-session-title status=passed\nagent.wait status=ok\nsession row key=agent:main:daily-fix-title-proof-1782883544408 autoTitle=\"TITLE PROOF OK\" derivedTitle=\"TITLE PROOF OK\"\nsessions.list search=\"TITLE\" matched=true matchedDerivedTitle=\"TITLE PROOF OK\"\n```\n\nFocused validation after the final async stale-write fix:\n\n- `targeted-tests-after-async-title-race-fix` — passed 14 focused test files / 841 tests covering session-title generation, reset/rollover stale-title cleanup, post-reply notification, auth-boundary, gateway search/event payload, UI filtering/event patching, and agent-facing session list behavior.\n- `typecheck-after-async-title-race-fix` — passed the core `tsgo -p tsconfig.core.json` check.\n- `architecture-after-async-title-race-fix` — passed import-cycle, deprecated API/JSDoc, Kysely, and database-first legacy-store guards.\n- `config-checks-after-async-title-race-fix` — passed config baseline and generated config schema checks.\n- Local ClawSweeper commit review for `13968bcce773d6b145e1c186c64ba9031216db19` returned `result: nothing_found` / `check_conclusion: success`.\n\nPost-submit remote state at the last check: `FAIL 0 / PENDING 0 / PASS 69 / SKIPPED 31`, `mergeStateStatus=CLEAN`, `mergeable=MERGEABLE`, and `proof: sufficient`. The `status: ⏳ waiting on author` label was still present, so a ClawSweeper re-review was requested.\n",
